From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Henrik Klee <henrik@goat-code.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] iio: apple-aop: Serve the T8010's gyroscope and pressure
 sensor

The A10's AOP firmware announces the same gyroscope and pressure
services as the A9's, and Apple's device trees for the iPad 5 (S8003)
and iPad 6 (T8010) describe both sensors with the same calibration
properties; the A10's AOP node is even compatible with the A9's
("iop,t8010", "iop,s8000"). The gyroscope and pressure drivers use only
the AOP service protocol: set-property requests, the calibration state
and the service's reports.

Bind them to the T8010's sensor nodes, which the T8010 device tree
already describes.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/iio/gyro/Kconfig                  | 2 +-
 drivers/iio/gyro/apple_aop_gyro.c         | 7 ++++---
 drivers/iio/pressure/Kconfig              | 3 ++-
 drivers/iio/pressure/apple_aop_pressure.c | 9 +++++----
 4 files changed, 12 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/iio/gyro/Kconfig b/drivers/iio/gyro/Kconfig
index 8f506a6..77f2180 100644
--- a/drivers/iio/gyro/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/iio/gyro/Kconfig
@@ -70,7 +70,7 @@ config APPLE_AOP_GYRO
 	select IIO_KFIFO_BUF
 	help
 	  Say yes here to get support for the gyroscope that the Always-On
-	  Processor (AOP) of Apple A9 iPads and iPhones serves.
+	  Processor (AOP) of Apple A9 and A10 iPads and iPhones serves.
 
 	  To compile this driver as a module, choose M here: the module will be
 	  called apple_aop_gyro.
diff --git a/drivers/iio/gyro/apple_aop_gyro.c b/drivers/iio/gyro/apple_aop_gyro.c
index edbda1f..3341164 100644
--- a/drivers/iio/gyro/apple_aop_gyro.c
+++ b/drivers/iio/gyro/apple_aop_gyro.c
@@ -2,9 +2,9 @@
 /*
  * Gyroscope served by the Apple Always-On Processor (AOP)
  *
- * The AOP firmware samples the gyroscope itself. Once it has the unit's
- * factory calibration and its batch, raw and report intervals (EPIC
- * set-property tags 0x16, 0x5c and 0), it sends one motion report (EPIC
+ * The AOP firmware of the A9 and A10 samples the gyroscope itself. Once it
+ * has the unit's factory calibration and its batch, raw and report intervals
+ * (EPIC set-property tags 0x16, 0x5c and 0), it sends one motion report (EPIC
  * subtype 0xc1) per report interval, laid out like the accelerometer's:
  *
  *   0  u16 sequence
@@ -273,6 +273,7 @@ static int apple_aop_gyro_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 
 static const struct of_device_id apple_aop_gyro_of_match[] = {
 	{ .compatible = "apple,s8000-aop-gyro" },
+	{ .compatible = "apple,t8010-aop-gyro" },
 	{ }
 };
 MODULE_DEVICE_TABLE(of, apple_aop_gyro_of_match);
diff --git a/drivers/iio/pressure/Kconfig b/drivers/iio/pressure/Kconfig
index 18535ad..fcdb9e1 100644
--- a/drivers/iio/pressure/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/iio/pressure/Kconfig
@@ -391,7 +391,8 @@ config APPLE_AOP_PRESSURE
 	select IIO_KFIFO_BUF
 	help
 	  Say yes here to get support for the barometric pressure sensor that
-	  the Always-On Processor (AOP) of Apple A9 iPads and iPhones serves.
+	  the Always-On Processor (AOP) of Apple A9 and A10 iPads and iPhones
+	  serves.
 
 	  To compile this driver as a module, choose M here: the module will be
 	  called apple_aop_pressure.
diff --git a/drivers/iio/pressure/apple_aop_pressure.c b/drivers/iio/pressure/apple_aop_pressure.c
index 8cd983c..70b1257 100644
--- a/drivers/iio/pressure/apple_aop_pressure.c
+++ b/drivers/iio/pressure/apple_aop_pressure.c
@@ -2,10 +2,10 @@
 /*
  * Barometric pressure sensor served by the Apple Always-On Processor (AOP)
  *
- * The AOP firmware samples the pressure sensor itself. Once it has the unit's
- * factory calibration and its batch, raw and report intervals (EPIC
- * set-property tags 0x16, 0x5c and 0), it sends one report (EPIC subtype
- * 0xc4) per report interval:
+ * The AOP firmware of the A9 and A10 samples the pressure sensor itself. Once
+ * it has the unit's factory calibration and its batch, raw and report
+ * intervals (EPIC set-property tags 0x16, 0x5c and 0), it sends one report
+ * (EPIC subtype 0xc4) per report interval:
  *
  *   0  u16 sequence
  *   2  u32 pressure in 1/65536 kPa
@@ -239,6 +239,7 @@ static int apple_aop_pressure_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 
 static const struct of_device_id apple_aop_pressure_of_match[] = {
 	{ .compatible = "apple,s8000-aop-pressure" },
+	{ .compatible = "apple,t8010-aop-pressure" },
 	{ }
 };
 MODULE_DEVICE_TABLE(of, apple_aop_pressure_of_match);
